Well, I'm just trying to look at the source... One thing I notice - the
probability of generating an item is 'per room' not 'per floor space'
- it's (if I read correctly) 1/3 for one item, 1/15 for two items,
1/75 for 3 items... Add to this the probability of generating a chest
(which could contain a WoW) - 40% per level. S we don't need to know 
the average floor space - the average number of rooms is enough.

Now probability that a randomly generated item is a wand is 4%, (6%
if generating in a container - chest, bag, etc) 

Probability that a randomly generated wand is a wand of wishing is 0.5%

You need of course much more information (average number of rooms/level,
probability of creating a container different than chest, average number
of items/container, probability of crating a monster folded with probability
that it will carry an item...) - but for a rough estimation this should
be enough. You'll see a WoW in the first room you enter once in ~15000
games (+higher-order corrections)

